course: dictionary
lesson: 5339
title: Khufu, the pharaoh who built a pyramid
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Khufu is a name, so it begins with a capital letter. It belongs to one person, a king of ancient Egypt. «The Great Pyramid was built about 4,500 years ago for the pharaoh Khufu.» The clues are pharaoh, which is a word for a king, and about 4,500 years ago, which tells you when he lived.
explain: «The Great Pyramid of Giza was built about 4,500 years ago for the pharaoh Khufu and was the tallest building in the world for nearly 4,000 years.» The word built and the word tomb tell you that Khufu had a huge tomb made for himself. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? A king's name fits, so Khufu is a king.
explain: Sometimes the same person has more than one name. The pyramid is often called the Pyramid of Khufu, and the Greeks called him Cheops. When you meet a new name in history, read the sentences around it, then check a dictionary or your teacher if you are still not sure.
fact: Khufu was a king, called a pharaoh, of ancient Egypt.
fact: Khufu lived about 4,500 years ago.
fact: The Great Pyramid of Giza was built as Khufu's tomb.
fact: The Greeks called Khufu Cheops.
fact: «Pharaoh» means a king of ancient Egypt.
exercise: Who was Khufu? | A Greek sailor who sailed the seas | A farmer who grew wheat by the river | A builder who made roads in Rome | *A king of ancient Egypt, called a pharaoh
exercise: «The Great Pyramid was built for the pharaoh Khufu.» What was the Great Pyramid built as? | A tall tower for ships | A castle for a Greek king | *A tomb for Khufu | A school for children
exercise: Find the word in «The Great Pyramid was built about 4,500 years ago for the pharaoh Khufu.» that tells you Khufu was a king. | *pharaoh | workers | pyramid | years
test: How long ago did Khufu live? | *About 4,500 years ago | About 45 years ago | About 4 years ago | About 450 years ago
test: The Greeks called Khufu by what other name? | Tomb | Giza | *Cheops | Pharaoh
exam: Why does Khufu start with a capital letter? | Because it is a very long word | *Because it is the name of a person | Because it is the first word of a sentence | Because it is an important place
